 "title": "Tax Sale Information / Dearborn County, Indiana",
 "text": "Tax Sale Information / Dearborn County, Indiana\nSkip over navigation\nDearborn County, Indiana\nA unique mixture of agriculture and industrial enterprises with easy access to surrounding areas\nHome\nAbout Us\nSite Tools\nSearch\nToggle Menu\nGovernment toggle Boards & Commissions Board of Health\nBoard of Zoning Appeals\nPark Board\nPlan Commission\nRedevelopment Commission\nRegional Sewer District Board\nSoutheast Regional Community Corrections Advisory Board\nSWCD Board of Supervisors\nCounty Commissioners\nCounty Council\nCounty Officials Assessor's Office\nAuditor's Office\nClerk of Courts\nCoroner's Office\nRecorder's Office\nSurveyor's Office\nTreasurer's Office\nDepartments A - M 911 Communications\nAnimal Control\nAssessor's Office\nAuditor's Office\nBuilding Department\nChild Support Program\nCircuit Court\nClerk of Courts\nCoroner's Office\nCounty Administrator\nCourt Services\nElections\nEmergency Management Agency\nGIS Services\nHealth Department\nHighway Department\nHuman Resources\nMS4\nDepartments N - Z Planning & Zoning\nProsecutor's Office\nRecorder's Office\nRecreation\nRecycling (Solid Waste Management District)\nRegional Sewer District\nSheriff's Office\nSoil & Water Conservation District\nSuperior Court I\nSuperior Court II\nSuveyor's Office\nTreasurer's Office\nVeterans Services\nElection Information\nCourts toggle Circuit Court\nSuperior Court I\nSuperior Court II\nClerk of Courts\nChild Support\nProsecutor\n>> More Court Information\nPublic Safety toggle 911 Communications\nAnimal Control\nEmergency Management\nSheriff's Department\n>> More Public Safety Information\nTaxes toggle Withholding Taxes\nAssessor's Office\nAssessment Appeals Process\nBusiness Personal Property\nProperty Search (GIS)\nTax Sale Information\n>> More Tax Information\nHealth toggle\nHealth Education\nEnvironmental Health\nPublic Health Prepardness\nHealth Officer\n>> More Health Information\nPermits toggle Building Permits\nHealth Permits\nHighway Permits\nZoning Permits\n>> More Permits\nRecreation\nFind It! toggle Ask a Question\nADA & Title VI Compliance\nEmployment Opportunities\nFind a Document\nFind a Permit\nFind a Service\nFrequently Asked Questions\nLearn More About Dearborn County\nSearch Locations & Facilities\nSubmit an Online Form\nTownship Trustees\nView Bids and Proposals\nView County Ordinances\nView the Events Calendar\nView the Image Gallery\nView the Staff Directory\n>> More Information / Links\nStart Content\nAssessor's Office\nYou are here: Home » Government » Assessor's Office » Tax Sale Information\nTax Sale Information\nOn or before July 1 of each year, the County Treasurer shall certify to the County Auditor, a list of real property with delinquent taxes that are eligible for tax sale.\nAny property taxes or special assessments certified to the County Auditor for collection by the County Treasurer from the prior year's spring installment or before are delinquent as determined under IC 6-1.1-37-10 or any unpaid costs from a prior tax sale (IC 6-1.1-24-1) shall be certified. Delinquent property taxes must exceed Twenty Five Dollars ($25).\nThe County Auditor shall maintain a list of all property eligible for sale. Unless the taxpayer pays to the County Treasurer all the amounts listed in the preceding paragraph, the taxpayer shall remain on the list. Click the appropriate listings button to view the most current list.\nA tract or item of real property may not be removed from the list certified before the tax sale unless all delinquent taxes, special assessments, penalties due on the delinquency, interest, and costs directly attributable to the tax sale have been paid in full. A county treasurer may accept partial payments of delinquent property taxes, assessments, penalties, interest, or costs after the list of real property is certified. For more information on parcels please contact the Auditor’s Office.\nClick here for Dearborn County Tax Sale Information (click on link and scroll to Dearborn County)\nContact Us\nAdministration Offices\n165 Mary St\nLawrenceburg, IN 47025\nGet Directions\nPhone: (812) 537-8811\nFax: (812) 532-3243\nStaff Directory\nOffice Hours:\nMonday - Friday 8:30am - 4:30pm\nTopics of Interest\nAssessment Appeals Process\nBusiness Personal Property Penalties\nTopic Home\nCyclical Review\nInheritance Tax\nProperty Cards\nProperty GIS Search\nSales Disclosure\nTax Sale Information\nJump to a topic or subtopic Make a Selection Assessment Appeals Process Business Personal Property --Penalties Cyclical Review Inheritance Tax Property Cards Property GIS Search Sales Disclosure Tax Sale Information Topic Home\nSite Design and Content Copyright © 2026 Dearborn County, Indiana\nSite Design and Content Management System by CORE Business Technologies\nPrivacy Policy\nAccessibility Statement\nTerms of Use",
